  "blocker": "The executable E2 closure and portable guarded-read components prove ordering and exact input binding only. Qman still lacks a product repository transaction that derives authority/read-set/CAS values itself, fences availability absence predicates, and commits the binding, lease, reservation, audit and idempotent result atomically.",
  "targetMilestone": "G1",
  "referenceEvidenceIds": ["QMAN-E2-CLOSURE-001"],
  "runner": {
    "cwd": "pci-resource-model",
    "argv": [
      "{python}",
      "-m",
      "unittest",
      "tests.test_c20_capability_closure"
    ]
  },
  "assertions": [
    "mandatory dependency action, exact qualification and reset contracts reach a bounded fixed point",
    "same-bundle free and busy inputs preserve bundle/capability/policy/snapshot hashes while changing decision availability",
    "missing or unauthenticated facts, stale snapshot identity, conflicts and closure overflow fail closed",
    "capability query performs no modeled bind, reset or lease write",
    "the admission command contains business intent only; the repository derives current vectors, predicate read sets, CAS expectations, lease specification and binding",
    "one serializable transaction prevents availability phantoms and commits either the complete admission lease/binding/reservation/idempotency/audit set or no row"
  ],
